>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `remove_iff`

``` hol4
clasimpLib.remove_iff : string -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes a persistent `[iff]` declaration by theorem name.

`remove_iff name` records a removal in the current theory and retracts both
the derived classical rules and the `srw_ss()` rewrite. An unqualified name
is resolved in the current theory when possible; a fully qualified database
name such as `"myTheory$my_iff"` can be supplied explicitly.

Removal is part of the theory's persistent iff declaration stream and is
therefore replayed and inherited through theory ancestry. It does not
delete the theorem from the theorem database.

### Failure

Removing an absent declaration has no effect. Name-resolution or theory
recording errors can still be reported.

### Example

``` hol4
clasimpLib.remove_iff "my_iff";
```

### See also

[`clasimpLib.iff`](#clasimpLib.iff),
[`clasetLib.Iff`](#clasetLib.Iff),
[`clasetLib.Del`](#clasetLib.Del)
